@title KuroFurtex

@image assets/img/portrait.png

@info
Species = Cat-wolf-fox hybrid
Origin = [[link:Kuromatria:kuromatria]]
Unlock = Unlocked By Default

@quote
Zyro's young brother. A joyful professional fella'. The owner of Kuromatria, before Zyro knocked him and take control the planet
- Description of KuroFurtex

@content
Kuro Furtex is the owner of [[link:Kuromatria:kuromatria]], a nice planet. He's also the default character you play in Rhythermia, since the game is about him. He has the character of chill person and professional being. He has a brother named [[link:Zyro Zytex:zyrozytex]]. which is the main antagonist of the game.

He's 17 years old. And he owns a weapon called Neolight Blade, which is the most powerful weapon in [[link:Kuromatria:kuromatria]].

# Appearance

He has the Appearance of White Furry with round head. He doesn't belongs to any species since he's identified as hybrid, which is a mixture of Cat, Wolf, and Fox. He wears basic Cyan shirt with blue leggings. He doesn't wear any shoes at all, yet he doesn't have any paws. But strangely enough, at some point, he does have paws, and it only appear when Kuro is being a cutie.

He has fluffy tail, and people do said that he's the most fluffiest person in the world. Not because of how spiky his fur is, but rather his fluffiness are at perfect balance between extreme fluffy and not fluffy.

# Lore & Stuff

As Main Owner of the planet [[link:Kuromatria:kuromatria]], he's also the legends of Neolight. he might not look intimidating, but don't let it fool you. He could go as fast as he wants, even at lightspeed. One slash are weak but millions of them in just a second is enough to cut literally everyone in debris. And also he's incredibly good at dodging.
[[img:Kuro's Reference Sheet:assets/img/kuro-ref.png]]
Born from his parents, Kyren and Selora. And raised by DiamondSpaceGD, also known as DSGD, Control of Reality. DSGD is one who formed [[link:Kuromatria:kuromatria]], and KuroFurtex is the one who's in charge of it. He obtained Neolight from DSGD and DSGD spread the Neolight around the planet, deep under the ground in the mantle layer, in form of crystals that Kuro can collect if he needs to.

Neolight Blade is his most used weapon and basically his primary weapon so far, it's pretty much lightweight yet enough to cut a literal Earth Mantle layer. The way he control this weapon is not by actually swinging it like a normal sword or any short-ranged weapon, but rather he swings it like a literal yo-yo, an incredibly long one. Due of it's feather weight, Kuro can pretty much swing it at incredible speed and it'll slash harder than normal.

The Neolight Blade he owned have infinite ways to expand. mainly he'll learn new SPECIALS that he can use in battle by simply observing world around and learn it's pattern. it worked similarly to TouHou's spell cards where such beautiful attack pattern is made but this one actually do harm and very flexible. Despite all possibility, there's multiple SPECIALS that Kuro mainly uses:
- CONTROLBLADE: Homings
- CONTROLBLADE: Train
- BLADEBITES
- CONTROLBLADE: Cloverleaf
- CONTROLBLADE: Axis Sphere
- MOONWIND

Aside from his blade, he also has modes/phase but oftentimes these phase only triggers on certain conditions, those modes include:
- Normal
- Darkside
- Crisis.

Crisis is the deadliest one where Kuro would basically breaks the limit which allows him to spawn more than 99 Quintillions Neolight Blade and also allows long-lasting SPECIALS to lasts for an entire year. But the only way to trigger this mode is basically shattering Kuro's trust and hopes into pieces to the point where depression hits him extremely that he wants the world to be gone.

# Trivia
- KuroFurtex always identify himself as "Shrodinger" (yea no I'm not calling him femboy)
- KuroFurtex's design were simplified because the creator himself finds small detail to be "unnessecary" for Kuro.
-- The Creator also want KuroFurtex to blend well at any artstyle, which explain his simplified design
- His Neolight Blade is fully reusable, which mean he'll never run out of his weapon.
- His Crisis mode did trigger once.
- Despite friendly converstation and interaction, Kuro however did not go well with Laera
